      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the 30-year-old woman in <Picture 1>, with a chin-length bob, a dark gray work jacket and a white hard hat with a lit headlamp.\n<Subject 2> is the carved-stone tunnel junction in <Picture 2>, seen looking into its left branch.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] Over the shoulder of <Subject 1>, luminous white mist rises from the floor of the left branch of <Subject 2> and rolls slowly outward toward her.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - seen from behind; hard hat, headlamp, hair and jacket are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the stone walls and floor of the left branch are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nCinematic live-action look with clean, gentle contrast and soft film grain; the mist is bright white and glowing, not gloomy. No subtitles or on-screen text. [Shot 1] Over-the-shoulder shot from just behind the right shoulder of <Subject 1>, her hard hat and shoulder soft in the right foreground, her headlamp beam reaching into the left branch of <Subject 2>. From the stone floor deep in the branch, a low layer of white mist begins to rise, thickening and glowing faintly from within, as if the passage were breathing out. It rolls forward along the floor in slow, layered waves, swallowing the beam's far end, and spreads toward her boots. She stays where she is; only her shoulder rises once with a slow breath. The camera drifts forward a few centimeters with the advancing mist, with a subtle handheld sway.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe drips stop. A soft, airy hiss like a long exhale fills the passage, under it the faint hum of the distant work lights.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
